explicitly test and rule out the replication-lag/miss hypothesis (mirror had refs/changes/* but the push for 2834 had not landed) before concluding live config was stale — and if lag was the cause, state what (retry/monitoring/pre-fetch-wait) actually addresses it rather than re-applying an already-live config.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the live mirror did not expose refs/changes/34/2834/1 during the incident, so the action fell back to Gerrit'","replication.config lines 33-34: 'falls back to fetching straight from Gerrit on replication lag'","replication.config lines 61-62: 'the checkout-gerrit-change-action gerrit-url fallback covers replication lag/misses'","The remediation (apply repo config) is a no-op if live config already contained refs/changes/* and the miss was lag, not a missing refspec"],"finding":"The plan's RCA fixes the 'live replication config is stale (missing refs/changes/*)' case but never rules out the competing hypothesis — documented in the config's own comments — that the mirror already had the refspec and replication merely LAGGED/MISSED for change 2834, which is precisely why the gerrit-url fallback exists. If the true cause was transient lag, applying the config does not solve the named problem.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f09fe12113cbe2230","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / RCA paragraph and Plan step 2 ('If live config is stale')","norm_id":"n307f818caa81ea87","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Live Gerrit config already had refs/changes/* applied via ADR-0021 change 49ad69b, but push for change 2834 was still in the retry queue / had failed when CI fetched"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_a